<title>RUSSIA: TABLE-Russia GDP falls 0.2 pct in Jan-July.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Russia GDP falls 0.2 pct in Jan-July.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian gross domestic product in the first seven months of this year totalled 1,454 trillion roubles, which was 0.2 percent less than a year earlier in inflation-adjusted terms, the State Statistics Committee said on Friday.</p>
<p>GDP in July was unchanged from a year earlier.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN GDP			  JUL 97    JUN 97    JUL 96</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change	+4.2	+3.6	+4.2</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change	   0.0	 0.0	-6.4</p>
<p>Note - Official Russian data tend to underreport a growing private sector in the economy.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
